TEST 8734 -- Neighbor Advertisement responses
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22 13:14:16  tb470
Method: send an ICMPv6 Neighbor Solicitation from tb470 eth2 for EACH IPv6
address the DUT holds on that VLAN, and require a Neighbor Advertisement back.

show ipv6 interface brief
Interface             IP-Address         Status          Protocol
lo            unassigned                      N/A          admin up    running
vlan1         fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f/64      preferred    admin up    running
vlan10        unassigned                      N/A          admin up    running
IE520-stk#--- DUT IPv6 addresses ---
    Interface             IP-Address         Status          Protocol
    lo            unassigned                      N/A          admin up    running
    vlan1         fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f/64      preferred    admin up    running
    vlan10        unassigned                      N/A          admin up    running

  addresses to solicit: ['fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f']

  NS -> fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f         NA received: 0  FAIL

VERDICT: see results above

NOTE: the NS is sent to the solicited-node multicast address with a source
link-layer option, i.e. a normal on-link neighbour discovery, not a crafted
unicast probe.

=== RETEST: solicited-node multicast computed from the TARGET address ===
The first run hardcoded the L2 destination as 33:33:ff:00:00:01, which does
not correspond to the target, so the NS was never accepted. That was an error
in the probe, not a DUT result.

show ipv6 interface brief
Interface             IP-Address         Status          Protocol
lo            unassigned                      N/A          admin up    running
vlan1         fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f/64      preferred    admin up    running
vlan10        unassigned                      N/A          admin up    running
IE520-stk#  targets: ['fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f']
  solicited-node: ff02::1:ff37:0d6f 33:33:ff:37:0d:6f
1
  NA from fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f | target fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f | R/S/O 0 1 1
    solicited-node: ff02::1:ff37:0d6f 33:33:ff:37:0d:6f
    1
    NA from fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f | target fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f | R/S/O 0 1 1
  => NS fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f : NA received 1  PASS

VERDICT: PASS -- every IPv6 address on the DUT answers its Neighbor Solicitation

SCOPE: the DUT holds ONE IPv6 address on the tested VLAN (the vlan1 link-local,
derived from the stack virtual MAC). vlan10 is IPv4-only and lo is unassigned,
so 'each IPv6 address' is one address here. Adding global addresses would
broaden the case but not change what it demonstrates.
